# CI gates before finish / commit (Cursor agents)

After any substantive code change under `src/`, `src-tauri/` that affects shared TS, i18n catalogs, or CI scripts — and **before**:

- declaring a plan or implementation “done” / complete
- creating a git commit (when the user explicitly asked to commit — see [no-unrequested-commits.mdc](no-unrequested-commits.mdc))
- pushing (when the user explicitly asked to push), if these gates were not just run clean

run and fix until green (same commands as the CI `typecheck` and `lint` jobs):

```bash
pnpm check
pnpm lint
pnpm check:tauri-commands
pnpm check:i18n-toasts
```

## Rules of engagement

- Do **not** treat failures in files you touched, or elsewhere on the current branch, as “pre-existing / out of scope” without verifying against `main`. Fix them, or stop and report the blocker.
- Docs-only / no-code turns follow [ask-when-no-code.mdc](ask-when-no-code.mdc) — skip this gate.
- Pure `src-tauri/` work: still run the four commands above if any `src/`, locale, or script CI cares about also changed. Rust unit tests remain as in `AGENTS.md`; this rule’s mandatory bar is the frontend CI gate that has been failing PRs.
- Report gate results briefly in the handoff (pass / fail + what you fixed).

This does not grant commit or push permission.
